@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@ As of version 0.33.29.1, migration 088 adds `note_library_collections.security_p
 
 As of version 0.33.29.2, migration 089 adds the durable catalog-transition action, monotonically increasing claim version, job and actor references, start time, and safe failure code. Notes repository operations condition ordinary catalog updates on the observed transition state/version, apply note and revision encryption/decryption in bounded adapter transactions, and finalize policy only when the same claim still owns the catalog. These columns contain no passwords, note bodies, encryption keys, secure payloads, or raw errors. The job row owns retry scheduling; the catalog row owns the fail-closed product state and rejects stale workers.
 
+In the reviewed adoption of the generated `adoption-sample` module (D3), migration 093 installs its one declared permission, `adoption_sample.view`, and grants it by default only to `super_admin` and `workspace_admin`. The consolidated baseline seeds the same rows, and the pre-adoption baseline checksum stays accepted so existing databases upgrade.
+
 As of version 0.33.31.11, migration 092 adds `public_demo_budget_usage`, keyed by `(workspace_id, user_id)`, with a nonnegative consumed-unit count and update timestamp plus a workspace/time index. The framework budget service changes this table only for exact marked public-demo visitors, serializes account and workspace limit checks with adapter transactions, releases reservations after denied or failed requests, and leaves successful reservations durable across an application restart. The external hourly database-and-Files baseline replacement clears the transient rows; normal installations keep the table empty.
 
 As of version 0.33.17.7.9, migration 074 changes Project Administrator from client scope to project scope. Each legacy client-scoped Project Administrator assignment is expanded to the existing projects in that same workspace/client with its permission overrides and timestamps preserved, the superseded client row is removed, and the canonical role metadata is updated to require project scope. A legacy client with no projects produces no replacement assignment because there is no project resource to authorize.
